From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herrie <github@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] luneos: launch through one helper, and name the app
 Waydroid

Two things the one-line launcher could not do.

It could not be closed. SAM tracks a native app by the process it spawned,
so a script that asked for the full UI and exited was never "running":
com.webos.applicationManager/close answered "is not running" while the card
sat on screen, and the launcher never showed Android as open.

And its id did not match its window. hwcomposer sets the Wayland app_id of
the full-UI window to "Waydroid", which luna-surfacemanager carries through
to WebOSSurfaceItem::appId, so a webOS app called id.waydro.container could
never be associated with the card it had just put up. Per-app windows use
"waydroid.<package>", which the generated per-app apps match, so this makes
the full UI follow the same rule instead of being the odd one out.

Both now go through /usr/libexec/waydroid-luneos-app, which holds the SAM
instance open for as long as Android has something on screen and turns SAM's
close into the right container-side action. It also carries the reason the
launcher has to ask "is a window shown" rather than "is the session running"
before calling show-full-ui, which is not idempotent.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS specific]
---
--- a/data/configs/luneos/appinfo.json
+++ b/data/configs/luneos/appinfo.json
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 {
-    "id": "id.waydro.container",
+    "id": "Waydroid",
     "title": "Waydroid",
     "version": "__VERSION__",
     "main": "waydroid.sh",
--- a/data/scripts/waydroid-luneos.sh
+++ b/data/scripts/waydroid-luneos.sh
@@ -1,3 +1,2 @@
 #!/bin/sh
-
-/usr/bin/waydroid show-full-ui
\ No newline at end of file
+exec /usr/libexec/waydroid-luneos-app
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 USE_NFTABLES ?= 0
 
 APP_ID := id.waydro.Container
-APP_ID_LUNEOS := id.waydro.container
+APP_ID_LUNEOS := Waydroid
 WAYDROID_DIR := $(PREFIX)/lib/waydroid
 BIN_DIR := $(PREFIX)/bin
 APPS_DIR := $(PREFIX)/share/applications
